Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: fix RK3576 suspend control

The RK3576 PHY suspend control is bits 8:0 of the port register, 0 for
normal operation and 0x1d1 for suspend, as in the Linux driver. U-Boot
only switched bits 1:0, so a PHY left suspended by the loader stayed
partly suspended (bits 4 and 6 still set), provided no UTMI clock, and the
DWC3 gadget failed with "failed to enable ep0out" (ums: -110).

---
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@
 		.clkout_ctl	= { 0x0008, 0, 0, 1, 0 },
 		.port_cfgs	= {
 			[USB2PHY_PORT_OTG] = {
-				.phy_sus	= { 0x0000, 1, 0, 2, 1 },
+				.phy_sus	= { 0x0000, 8, 0, 0, 0x1d1 },
 			}
 		},
 	},
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@
 		.clkout_ctl	= { 0x2008, 0, 0, 1, 0 },
 		.port_cfgs	= {
 			[USB2PHY_PORT_OTG] = {
-				.phy_sus	= { 0x2000, 1, 0, 2, 1 },
+				.phy_sus	= { 0x2000, 8, 0, 0, 0x1d1 },
 			}
 		},
 	},
